{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nS1 proves one atomic update executor and S2 produces pure plans, but legacy batch dispatch still replays compound methods, conflates deferred and applied work, and has no endpoint-failure fuse and relies on ad-hoc nested per-call retries that cannot distinguish physical attempts from exhausted logical outcomes (the only breaker today is the blast-radius mass-mutation guard `classify.check_blast_radius`, which is a different concern). One ticket-local or permanent failure can distort batch behavior.\n\n## Outcome\nMake the typed coordinator authoritative for non-create plans: update, delete, probe, clean-label, repair-property, and conflict handling. Execute atomic desired postconditions in dependency order; after partial success, re-observe and plan only remaining drift. Produce exact ticket/pass outcomes and apply the approved endpoint/provider finite-pass fuse only to normalized exhausted logical failures.\n\n## Plan\n1. Add a coordinator that consumes immutable plans, enforces dependencies, and calls adapter atomic operations through S1s budget. Preserve successful earlier postconditions and never replay the whole compound mutation after a late failure.\n2. Normalize auto-healed, success, deferred, permanent, commit-unknown, exhausted transient, and skipped dispositions with ticket/endpoint/tenant/provider/global scope.\n3. Add a new endpoint-failure scoped fuse (none exists today). Endpoint scope opens after three consecutive eligible exhausted logical outcomes across at least two tickets; provider scope additionally requires the failing outcomes to span >=2 distinct endpoints of the same provider. A matching success resets consecutive state. The existing blast-radius mass-mutation guard (`classify.check_blast_radius`) is a distinct protection and is retained unchanged.\n4. Exclude physical attempts, recovered warnings, permanent failures, ticket-local 404, and opaque diagnostics from inferred fuse counters. Retain direct authoritative credential, configuration, quota, rate, issue, endpoint, tenant, and global behavior.\n5. When a fuse opens, defer remaining matching plans with reason/scope/retry metadata while independent scopes continue. Preserve exact applied/failed/deferred/skipped tallies and nonzero degraded-pass signaling.\n\n## Testing (RED → GREEN)\n- Coordinator tables cover dependency success/failure, partial compound update, idempotent already-gone delete, ticket-local 404 isolation, permanent 4xx, auth/quota/rate scopes, and mixed endpoints of one provider.\n- Fuse sequences assert threshold, two-ticket/two-distinct-endpoint requirements, success reset, exclusions, and independent-scope continuation.\n- Replay fixtures derived from historical GitHub Actions outcomes assert zero premature stop in the completed 1,200-run slice; raw warning/grep text is never classified as a terminal outcome.\n- Verified-fake Cloud/DC batches assert wire order, maximum calls, exact tallies, logs, and exit status.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nCut over by non-create operation family and never dual-send. Before legacy removal, an operation-family flag can select the old dispatcher. Rollback preserves successful Jira effects and resumes from re-observation. The intentional differences are three-call shared budgeting, explicit deferral, exact partial outcomes, and a new endpoint-failure scoped fuse (the blast-radius mass-mutation guard is retained).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Non-create plans execute atomic postconditions once in dependency order; a late failure preserves earlier success and re-observes only remaining drift within the same logical budget.\n- [ ] Ticket-local/permanent failures isolate the ticket, authoritative broad scopes stop only their declared scope, and independent tickets/endpoints continue.\n- [ ] Endpoint fuse opens only after three consecutive eligible exhausted logical outcomes across two tickets; provider fuse additionally requires >=2 distinct endpoints of the same provider; matching success resets state.\n- [ ] Physical attempts, recovered warnings, permanent failures, ticket-local 404s, and opaque diagnostics never increment inferred fuse counters.\n- [ ] Remaining matching work is explicitly deferred with reason/scope/`retry_not_before`; applied, failed, deferred, skipped, and recovered tallies plus exit status are exact.\n- [ ] Historical replay fixtures and verified-fake Cloud/DC batches show no premature termination of observed successful/partially successful work.\n\n## Fuse scope, eligibility & counter semantics (resolves E2/G6)\nGrounded entirely in existing `operation_outcome` types — no new \"family\" concept.\n- **Endpoint / provider.** *Endpoint* = one concrete provider instance the coordinator dispatches to (a single Jira base URL/site), the unit `FailureScope.endpoint` already denotes; *provider* = the vendor behind ≥1 endpoints (`FailureScope.provider`).\n- **Attribution.** `OperationOutcome` carries `logical_id` + authoritative `failure_scope` but no endpoint id, so the **coordinator** (the adapter's caller) tags each outcome with the `(provider, endpoint)` it dispatched to; inferred counters key off that identity, never off diagnostic text. A direct authoritative `failure_scope` of endpoint/tenant/provider/global still stops that scope immediately (step 4), independent of the counter.\n- **Eligible exhausted outcome** = the op consumed its full per-pass retry budget from transient causes and terminated the pass without the desired postcondition. Per `retry_budget.py` that is `exhausted_transient` (MAX_INVOCATIONS, or `old_conclusive` with no budget) **and** terminal `retryable_deferred` (cumulative-sleep cap `MAX_CUMULATIVE_SLEEP_MS` hit before MAX_INVOCATIONS — the slow/rate-limited mode that never surfaces `exhausted_transient`). Only the terminal `retryable_deferred` counts; the mid-loop `decide_replay(old_conclusive, budget_remaining=True)` variant (`replay=True`) is never a pass outcome. **Excluded** (step 4): `commit_unknown` (opaque/replay-forbidden), `recovered`, `already_satisfied`, `permanent_failure`, ticket-local 404, raw physical attempts.\n- **Counter durability/order.** Per-pass, in-memory, per-scope; zeroed each `reconcile_once(pass_id)` pass (no durable cross-pass state, consistent with S2's fresh Observation/version). \"Consecutive\" is per-scope over the coordinator's deterministic dependency-ordered execution; other scopes' interleaved outcomes neither increment nor reset a scope's counter (so independent scopes continue). A same-scope success (`applied`/`recovered`/`already_satisfied`) resets that scope to zero.\n- **Thresholds.** Endpoint opens after 3 consecutive eligible outcomes across ≥2 tickets on that endpoint within the pass; provider additionally requires ≥2 distinct endpoints of that provider. On open, remaining matching plans defer with reason/scope/`retry_not_before`; independent scopes keep running. A persistently-bad endpoint re-trips each pass that alone reaches threshold."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787628724488971001,"uuid":"69fae3d1-2aaf-4628-b5a4-e5e667cfecc4"}